{"title":"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Probability_States)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Probability States)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bag contains two red beads and two green beads. You reach into the bag and pull out a bead, replacing it with a red bead regardless of the color you pulled out. What is the probability that all beads in the bag are red after three such replacements?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/435f1a9ce0a4600bca8dffe6c881084219ab8adb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{8} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{5}{32} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{9}{32} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{3}{8} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{7}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"399\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Casework)\">Solution 1 (Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can divide the case of all beads in the bag being red after three replacements into three cases. \n</p><p>The first case is in which the two green beads are the first two beads to be chosen. The probability for this is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c79094610c98c663ffb3d62502cdcc8d8e4bea3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{4}{4} = \\frac{1}{8}\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>The second case is in which the green beads are chosen first and third. The probability for this is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73ceeaa46918d0f91fc747ff8f6a3fbc52989dad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{4} \\times \\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{3}{32}\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The third case is in which the green beads are chosen second and third. The probability for this is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892342fa379797a31251d5885c6957b04e601ee8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{4} \\times \\frac{2}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{16}\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Add all these cases together\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b582cc507ddc9c4ad70f25708252281aeab43997.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{3}{32}+\\frac{1}{16} = \\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{3}{32}+\\frac{2}{32} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) \\ } \\frac{9}{32}}\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Probability_States.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Probability_States)\">Solution 2 (Probability States)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Probability States)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use probability states. Notice that we can construct a Markov chain like the one below.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sol22023amc10bq21.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a8/Sol22023amc10bq21.png/850px-Sol22023amc10bq21.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"850\" height=\"203\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a8/Sol22023amc10bq21.png/1275px-Sol22023amc10bq21.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/a8/Sol22023amc10bq21.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>From this, each arrow represents one distinct replacement. Then, one can notice that we can loop from 2 Red to 2 Red, and then move from 2 Red to 3 Red and from 3 Red to All red. However another case is to go from 2 Red to 3 Red directly, and loop once at 3 Red, and move to 4 Red. The third case is to immediately in two moves go from 2 Red to 3 Red, and then from 3 Red to 4 Red, and to loop at 4 Red.\n</p><p>The first case has a probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae39aea9724654c2995a18114df416d1be3fbf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />. The second case has a probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f12c83c8239d31b43e4a575eebcd0fd901f25d0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{3}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />. The third case has probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2accb88b504250fe6bcd15ba23bdcd6e1c8329d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 1 = \\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The asked probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/9844be726980d068ed1aaaccc224d322090848a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{32} + \\frac{3}{32} + \\frac{4}{32} = \\boxed{\\frac{9}{32}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"170\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B\">2003 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title